<MudContainer MaxWidth="MaxWidth.Medium" Class="mt-6">

    <MudText Typo="Typo.h4" GutterBottom="true">
        Manufacturer Manager
    </MudText>

    <MudCard Elevation="3" Class="p-6 mud-card">

        <MudText GutterBottom="true">
            This is an application for managing manufacturers
            and the widgets that they produce.
        </MudText>

        <MudText GutterBottom="true">
            ManufacturerManager started life as a straightforward Blazor CRUD app for managing manufacturers and their widgets.
            It has since grown into something a little more interesting.
        </MudText>

        <MudText GutterBottom="true">
            Alongside the usual clean architecture, MudBlazor components, and tidy domain modelling, it now includes:
        </MudText>

        <MudList T="string">

            <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Circle">
                <strong>RAG‑powered AI</strong> that understands the application’s own data
            </MudListItem>

            <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Circle">
                <strong>Natural‑language‑to‑SQL</strong>, so you can ask questions instead of writing queries
            </MudListItem>

            <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Circle">
                A UI designed to be pleasant rather than performative
            </MudListItem>

            <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Circle">
                A structure that favours clarity over cleverness
            </MudListItem>

        </MudList>
            
            <MudText>
                It’s still a relatively simple application at heart — just one with a few carefully‑placed “gotchas”
                to demonstrate how I think about architecture, extensibility, and developer experience.
            </MudText>

        <MudText>
            GitHub: <MudLink href="https://github.com/JulianAburrow/ManufacturerManager" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ManufacturerManager</MudLink>
        </MudText>

    </MudCard>

</MudContainer>